Maplet is an independent mapping library inspired by Leaflet. This notice
records Leaflet-derived calculations and techniques from the earlier
leaflet-gpu prototype.

Leaflet
-------
The coordinate math in `src/math/crs.ts` (spherical Web Mercator x/y, the
85.0511287798 degree latitude limit, longitude wrapping into [-180, 180) and the
"256 x 2^zoom" world scale convention) is derived from Leaflet 1.9.4
(https://leafletjs.com, L.Projection.SphericalMercator, L.CRS, L.LatLng wrap and
bounds behavior). Tests in `test/math/crs.test.ts` compare the preserved contracts
against the real Leaflet 1.9.4 build as an independent oracle.
The unmodified ESM test oracle is included at `demo/vendor/leaflet.esm.js`,
with Leaflet's stylesheet at `demo/vendor/leaflet.css` for comparison pages.
These are development dependencies only, not part of the published package.

