Demo tiles and test services
----------------------------
`demo/tiles/` and `demo/tiles-svg/` are generated fixtures (part of this
repository, covered by the root LICENSE); they encode tile coordinates and test patterns and are not
derived from any map data.

`demo/tiles-providers/` is an optional one-time offline cache fetched by
`demo/fetch-tiles.py` for deterministic browser checks (`demo/tiles.html`).
It is ignored by Git and is not part of the published package (`package.json#files`). The tiles
remain the property of their providers and must be attributed when displayed:

- OSM-DE style: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, openstreetmap.de style -
  https://www.openstreetmap.de/germanstyle.html
- OpenTopoMap: (c) OpenTopoMap (CC-BY-SA) - https://opentopomap.org/about#faq
- Esri World Imagery: Powered by Esri - Source: Esri, Maxar, Earthstar
  Geographics, and the GIS User Community

The demo also requests live tiles from public providers exactly like Leaflet's
quick start (`L.tileLayer(url, { maxZoom, attribution })`):

- OpenStreetMap standard: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors -
  https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/ ; the operations team
  blocks scripted fetching of this layer (it answers with a block tile at
  HTTP 200), so the demo only uses it live from the browser and
  `demo/fetch-tiles.py` refuses to cache it (duplicate-payload detection);
- Carto Positron was dropped from the demo because anonymous requests now
  return an "API KEY REQUIRED" placeholder image.

Font fixtures
-------------
`demo/fonts/maplet-subset.woff2` is a Roboto glyph subset (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright 2011 Google Inc.) fetched by `demo/fetch-font.py` from the Google
Fonts CSS API (`text=` subsetting). It contains only the glyphs of the browser
font checks plus U+0301; details and the regeneration command are in
`demo/fonts/NOTICE.txt`. It is a development fixture for `demo/fonts.html` and
is not part of the published package.

Media fixtures
--------------
`demo/media/` is generated by `demo/generate-media.py`: `corners.png` and
`corners-alt.png` are hand-encoded 8×8 RGBA bitmaps (no third-party data) and
`two-frames.mp4` is a two-frame solid-colour video encoded with `ffmpeg`
(if installed). They are development fixtures for `demo/media.html` and are
not part of the published package.

leaflet-gpu prototype
---------------------------------------
The following techniques were ported from the `leaflet-gpu` prototype and are
re-verified by Maplet's own fixtures, not inherited as trust:

- polygon ear-clipping and hole subtraction in `src/render/triangulate.ts`;
- instanced batched attributes, chunk-local Mercator origins and the dash-in-
  fragment-shader approach in the WebGL 1 renderer;
- radix/ordering ideas behind the incremental spatial index.

Unchanged behavior of the prototype is not promised. The public API, identity
model, transactions, relations and bindings are new and are not part of the
prototype.

Leaflet's name and the `L.*` API are not used at runtime; Maplet has no runtime
dependency on Leaflet. Inspiration and the derivation of specific calculations
do not imply API compatibility.
